  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Dangerous heat expected much of the time through \nmid next week.\n\nMid-level high pressure will generally prevail across the region \naiding in above normal temperatures near record levels at times. \nHigh humidity will help push heat indices into Heat Advisory range \n(105-109 degrees) for most each day and even into Heat Warning range \n(110+ degrees) for some (mainly across the coastal counties where \ndewpoints should be greatest due to the sea breeze). However, it is \nworth noting that forecast confidence regarding heat indices remains \nlower than normal, especially this weekend, as there is some \nuncertainty regarding temps/dewpoints/rain/cloud coverage. \n\nRemember, heat is the #1 weather-related cause of death so everyone \nis encouraged to take proper precautions. Check out our heat page \n(weather.gov/ilm/heat) for the latest heat forecasts and safety \ninfo. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Minor coastal flooding likely into early next week \nalong the lower Cape Fear River.\n\nHigh astronomical tides and continued tidal anomalies will lead to \nminor coastal flooding along the lower Cape Fear River through \ntoday, potentially during both the daytime and nighttime high\ntides.",
